This license covers MirrorMe's own source code only (the Go application and
its frontend). It does not cover native receiver or third-party library
code. Those components retain their own licenses.

The legacy receiver is a separate GPLv3 program, with source in receiver/.
The self-contained native build statically links GPL-licensed AirPlay
protocol code into the application; that combined executable must be
distributed under the applicable GPL terms, including corresponding
source. This does not remove the MIT grant for MirrorMe's own Go/frontend
source considered separately. See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md before
